  <section class="blk" style="border-bottom:0">
    <h2>6 · What has been read, and found empty</h2>
    <ul class="dek" style="margin-bottom:1.2rem">
      <li><span class="chip inf">newly opened · 10 Sep 2026</span> <strong>Is Sneyd-street, Bowen
      Hills, named for the gaol governor?</strong> The street surfaced by accident in a 1902
      insolvency notice. Bowen Hills sits in the <strong>Parish of North Brisbane</strong>, and
      Samuel Sneyd was mortgaging subdivisions in that parish in <strong>1870 and 1872</strong>
      (QSA <span class="mono">ITM3248152</span>, <span class="mono">ITM3622143</span>). Subdividers
      named the streets they cut. <strong>The subdivision plan would settle it</strong>, and it is
